  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 214 PM CDT Sun Oct 25 2026\n\nAn upper level trough is over much of the Rocky Mountains and \nextends eastward over portions of Nebraska and Kansas. This has \nbrought an increase in upper lift over the region which has resulted \nin rain showers approaching the forecast area from the west. Winds \nacross south central and central Nebraska and north central Kansas \nare mainly out of the east at around 5 to 10 MPH. High temperatures \ntoday are expected to range from the 50s to the 70s. The rain \nshowers and maybe some isolated thunderstorms will spread eastward \nacross the forecast area this afternoon through tonight. Low \ntemperatures tonight will mostly be in the 40s and 50s. Some upper \n30s may occur across northwestern portions of Valley County. \n\nThe upper trough will be over the region on Monday with winds \nbeginning to switch to the northwest and north across western and \nnorthern portions of the area. High temperatures are expected to \nrange from the 50s to the 70s although there is some uncertainty due \nto the timing and positioning of the cold front. Rain showers and \nthunderstorms will continue across the area Monday into Monday \nevening. Rain will be coming to an end Monday night. Western and \nnorthwestern portions of the forecast area are expected to see the \nhighest rainfall amounts with this system (around 1 to near 1.40 \ninches). Low temperatures Monday night are expected to range from as \nlow as the upper 20s to the low 50s. \n\nA surface high will remain near the area on Tuesday allowing for \ntemperatures to remain cooler (highs ranging from the 50s to low \n70s). Light rain may develop across the area Tuesday evening and \nnight (15% to 30% chance) with a broad upper trough over the region. \nWednesday appears to be dry across the area with high temperatures \nin the 60s and 70s. Similar conditions are expected Thursday. Rain \nchances increase (up to around 60%) on Friday and Saturday as upper \nlift increases over the region. High temperatures in the 60s and 70s \nare expected Friday with highs mainly in the 60s on Saturday.",
